{
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": { "level": 1 },
      "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Heidi Negotiates With the Alps" }]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The Swiss Alps did not ask for a publicist, but they got Heidi anyway. Somewhere between a cowbell and a postcard, she is still winning the argument about fresh air in "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "link",
              "attrs": {
                "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swiss_Alps",
                "target": "_blank",
                "rel": "noopener noreferrer",
                "class": "link"
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Switzerland"
        },
        { "type": "text", "text": "." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Flag_of_Switzerland.svg/330px-Flag_of_Switzerland.svg.png",
        "alt": "The flag of Switzerland, a white cross on a red square",
        "title": "Swiss flag",
        "align": "left",
        "width": 140,
        "fileName": null
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The flag is a square on purpose. Heidi tried a rectangle once. The cross filed a complaint, and the mountains sided with the cross."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [{ "type": "italic" }],
          "text": "The meadow is complimentary. The cheese takes itself very seriously."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": { "level": 2 },
      "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "The person who wrote the meadow down" }]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Johanna Spyri put Heidi on the page. The Alps have been insufferable about it ever since, which is their most reliable personality trait."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Johanna_Spyri_21j%C3%A4hrig_2.jpg/960px-Johanna_Spyri_21j%C3%A4hrig_2.jpg",
        "alt": "Portrait of Johanna Spyri, who wrote Heidi",
        "title": "Johanna Spyri",
        "align": "right",
        "width": 280,
        "fileName": null
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Spyri did the difficult part: she made fresh air sound like a plot. Heidi still clocks in. The wildflowers do not."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": { "level": 2 },
      "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Maienfeld, unofficial headquarters" }]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Down in Maienfeld the Heidi fountain keeps the village's version of the story. The water is cold. The legend is not."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Heidibrunnen_in_Maienfeld_01.jpg/960px-Heidibrunnen_in_Maienfeld_01.jpg",
        "alt": "The Heidi fountain in Maienfeld",
        "title": "Heidibrunnen, Maienfeld",
        "align": "center",
        "width": 640,
        "fileName": null
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": { "level": 2 },
      "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "A short field guide" }]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Heidi's office has excellent views and questionable management. Bring layers, and do not argue with the goats."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Matterhorn_from_Domh%C3%BCtte_-_2.jpg/960px-Matterhorn_from_Domh%C3%BCtte_-_2.jpg",
        "alt": "The Matterhorn, looking as if it practiced this pose",
        "title": "Matterhorn",
        "align": "center",
        "width": 720,
        "fileName": null
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletList",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                { "type": "text", "marks": [{ "type": "bold" }], "text": "Matterhorn" },
                { "type": "text", "text": " — the mountain that refuses to sit up straight, and knows it." }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                { "type": "text", "text": "A meadow with a job description. Heidi clocks in. The wildflowers do not." }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                { "type": "text", "text": "One thermos. Even a wholesome Alpine story eventually needs coffee." }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "blockquote",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            { "type": "text", "marks": [{ "type": "bold" }], "text": "Local guide:" },
            { "type": "text", "text": " If you yodel, the echo yodels back. That is not encouragement. That is acoustics." }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "horizontalRule" },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Heidi would like the record to show that the Alps are lovely, the goats believe they are in charge, and the mountains already scheduled that pleasantly small feeling before breakfast."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
